<title>UK: KEXIM ups to $650 mln and prices 10-yr bond,+51 bp.</title>
<headline>KEXIM ups to $650 mln and prices 10-yr bond,+51 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by lead manager Lehman Brothers, has been priced and increased to $650 million from $500 million.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EXPORT-IMPORT BANK OF KOREA</p>
<p> AMT    $650 MLN	COUPON     7.10 PCT  MATURITY   *15.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.852    PAY DATE   S25.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  30 BP     REOFFER    99.852    SPREAD	+51 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	A1	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) ONE     SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/KR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    N.Y	 HOME CTRY  KOREA     TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    5 BP	SELL CONC  25 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND FIVE YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES     *PUT AT PAR AFTER FIVE YEARS. S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
